    "title": "Texas A&M basketball vs Houston game score: Aggies season ends in OKC",
    "text": "OKLAHOMA CITY — Texas A&M men's basketball was simply outmatched Saturday as its season ended at the hands of Houston, 88-57.Watch MoreThe 10th-seeded Aggies trailed the second-seeded Cougars 46-28 at halftime after holding a lead for only 2 minutes and 50 seconds during the first frame. They never regained that lead and finished the first half shooting 1-for-13 from the field. It wasn't much better in the second half, where they shot just 34.8%.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢A&M (22-12) was never able to bring the deficit below 20 in the second half, as the Cougars kept dominating on the glass and continued to prove why they’re one of the best teams in the country.Houston guard Kingston Flemings (center) fights for a rebound against Texas A&M forward Jamie Vinson (right) during the first half in the second round of the NCAA college basketball tournament in Oklahoma City, Saturday, March 21, 2026.Brett Coomer/Houston ChronicleA&M was outrebounded 46-29 and struggled with fouls, getting called for 20 compared to Houston's 16. The Aggies were crushed in the paint, 32-20 and in second-chance points, 18-8. A&M reserve guard Josh Holloway had a team-high 12 points. Forward Jamie Vinson paced the Aggies on the boards with six rebounds.Article continues below this adLikely NBA lottery pick Kingston Flemings was held to just nine points. But Houston (30-6) got major contributions from fellow Emanuel Sharp, who led all scorers with 18 points, and Chris Cenac Jr. who had 17 points on just nine field goal attempts and had a game-high nine rebounds.The Cougars head to the Sweet 16 for the sixth straight year. They'll face the No. 3 Illinois at Toyota Center later this week.Final updates from the action:Article continues below this ad Texas A&M basketball vs Houston: Live updates from NCAA Tournament Final: Houston 88, Texas A&M 57 3:58, 2H: Houston 80, Texas A&M 55 With just under four minutes remaining, it looks like the Aggies' season will end in the Round of 32. Houston continues to assert their dominance, widening the lead to 25 at the final media timeout of the game.Article continues below this ad 7:56, 2H: Houston 73, Texas A&M 49 The Aggies continue to battle but continue to struggle against a superior Cougars squad, who has an answer for every punch A&M has thrown. 11:52, 2H: Houston 64, Texas A&M 39 Simply put: A&M has been outclassed so far. Houston continues to shoot, rebound, and hustle better. Many expected this since the Aggies were heavy favorites, but a lot has to change quickly if the maroon and white want to keep their season alive.Article continues below this ad 15:53, 2H: Houston 56, Texas A&M 33 Coming out of the break, the struggles continued for the Aggies as the Cougars extended their lead to 23. A&M is shooting just 33% from the field this half, while Houston is maintaining a strong 50%. Halftime: Houston 46, Texas A&M 28 4:16, 1H: Houston 35, Texas A&M 24 Houston has started to pull ahead with a 10-0 run that forced an A&M timeout. The Aggies missed their last six shots and haven't scored in over three minutes. Article continues below this ad 8:37, 1H: Houston 25, Texas A&M 21 The foul disparity is pretty large right now, with the Aggies getting called for eight while the Cougars have been called for four. One of A&M's fouls was a technical, while Dominguez was called for a flagrant-one for an elbow to the head or neck area. 10:53, 1H: Houston 17, Texas A&M 13 A 9-0 run helped lift the Cougars to their first lead of the game. Houston has been dominating the offensive glass, 10-2. Frustration early as the A&M bench got called for a technical due to some borderline over-the-back calls that went the Cougars way.Article continues below this ad 15:11, 1H: Texas A&M 10, Houston 9 The intensity is high early on, with both teams playing at a fast pace from end to end. The difference is that the Aggies are shooting 44% from the field, while the Cougars are at 33%. Texas A&M basketball starting lineup G - Marcus Hill G - Pop Isaacs G - Rylan Griffen G - Ruben Dominguez F - Rashaun Agee Article continues below this ad Houston basketball starting lineup G - Kingston Flemings G - Milos Uzan G - Emanuel Sharp F - Joseph Tugler C - Chris Cenac Jr. Texas A&M basketball vs Houston time, TV info When: 5:10 p.m.Article continues below this adWhere: Paycom Center, Oklahoma CityTV/radio: TNT, 1370 AM in Austin; 1150 AM, 93.7 FM in College Station. Texas A&M vs Houston basketball betting odds Odds as of Saturday, per BetMGMArticle continues below this adMoneyline: Texas A&M +400, Houston -550Spread: Texas A&M is a 10½ point underdogOver/under: 142½Article continues below this adReach Texas A&M beat reporter Tony Catalina via email at Anthony.Catalina@statesman.com.Statesman LogoGet the hookup and your Horns Up with Longhorns coverage.March 21, 2026Texas A&M Beat ReporterTony Catalina is the Texas A&M beat reporter for the Austin American-Statesman. He is a Heisman Trophy voter from Worcester, Mass., with more than five years of sports reporting experience. He previously worked at SB Nation, Pro Football Network and New England Football Journal, where he covered NFL, college and high school football before joining the Statesman. Before pursuing a career in journalism, Catalina served as a high school football coach in Massachusetts and, in 2016, was a recruiting analyst for the University of Georgia football program under head coach Kirby Smart.",
